{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he looked, and behold, a well in the field.</b> In each of the Patriarchs we find wells, and in each of them the future is alluded to. In the matter of Isaac Scripture called it (Genesis 26:19) ״באר מים חיים״ — a well of living waters; and the matter in all of them is that the well alludes to the Holy Temple (beit ha-mikdash) that is destined to be built from their seed, and it likened the Holy Temple to a well because from there Torah would go forth, and Torah was likened to water." "<b>And behold, there were three flocks of sheep.</b> It could have said simply 'and behold, three flocks of sheep,' and it added the word 'there' (שם) in the manner of what Scripture says (Ezekiel 3:23): ״והנה שם כבוד ה׳ עומד״ — 'and behold, there stood the glory of HaShem.' And Israel are called the flock of the Place (HaMakom), as it is written (Ezekiel 34:31): ״ואתנה צאני צאן מרעיתי״. And it is written (Psalms 79:13): ״ואנחנו עמך וצאן מרעיתך״. And it mentioned three because Israel are three divisions: priests, Levites, and Israelites, and they would go up there three times a year." "<b>For from that well they would water the flocks, and the stone.</b> Here is alluded the Name engraved in the Holy Temple (beit ha-mikdash): 'for from that well they would water' — for from there they would draw the Holy Spirit, blessed be He (ru'ach ha-kodesh); and the great stone is the great golden crown, it is the 'four' (ד׳) of the One, it is the final 'five' (ה׳) that is in the Name, upon the mouth of the well, at the entrance of the Temple."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {2 "The Kabbalistic phrase 'ארבע של אחד היא ה אחרונה' is rendered hyper-literally; the allusion to the divine Name is deliberately cryptic and left undecoded per instructions. The trailing phrase 'על פי הבאר, על פתח המקדש' presents textual ambiguity regarding the reading of 'על פי'; translated literally without resolving."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:06.209432178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}